MGA-Glide local patch 0117: what the G-series' 2D engine, cursor and CRTC do
that 86Box's model did not, found writing the HAL's 2D primitives for GLOS M7
(MGA-Glide docs/matrox-2d.md, which cites the specifications):

- A BITBLT on the G200 and later reads its source at SRCORG + AR3 (SRCORG in
  bytes, 32-byte units on the G200 and 64 on the G400; AR3 in pixels, or bits
  for one-bit sources). The model read at AR3 alone. X.org's EXA driver
  depends on SRCORG, and the HAL uses it to keep AR0 within the 18 bits the
  G200 specification gives it.
- CRTCEXT0 bit 6 is bit 20 of the display start on the G100, G200 and G400
  (starts past 8 MB).
- XCURADDH has 6 bits on the G200 and G400 (a cursor image anywhere in the
  first 16 MB); the model kept the G100's 5.
- The cursor colours (XCURCOLn: R, G, B) were drawn with red and blue
  swapped, and in XGA mode through the palette (other colours at 16 bits a
  pixel); the three-colour mode (XCURCTRL 01) drew nothing; and the cursor
  was 32 lines tall, the SVGA core's default, not 64.

